From a74fc143b97090bfedee3843045f230d778d745d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 07:13:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: billing & invoicing (WIP, invoice generation/lifecycle,
 realization rate)

Closes the loop between work happening (time entries) and revenue
capture (invoices), the highest-leverage gap identified in the Q1
roadmap: the system tracked cost but not revenue capture.

Backend:
- Invoice / InvoiceLineItem models. TimeEntry gains
  invoice_line_item_id (null = still WIP); User gains
  standard_billing_rate as the fallback rate when a project's
  contract doesn't carry an hourly_rate.
- app/core/billing.py: rate resolution (contract hourly_rate -> user
  standard rate -> unrated), compute_wip(), compute_realization()
  grouped by project/partner/department.
- /invoices routes: generate from WIP time entries and/or manual
  line items -> send -> record-payment (supports partial payments)
  -> void (releases entries back to WIP) -> delete (draft only);
  plus /invoices/wip.
- /reports/realization: billed-vs-worked rate by engagement,
  partner, or department, with firm-wide rollup.
- PATCH /users/{email}/billing-rate (admin-only) to set a user's
  standard rate.
- Department-scoped write permissions wired in via the existing
  require_scoped_write pattern.
- Alembic migration e5f6a7b8c9d0, verified upgrade -> downgrade ->
  re-upgrade against a pre-change schema snapshot.

Tests: 31 new tests (WIP valuation, rate fallback, invoice
generation/lifecycle, void-releases-WIP, permission boundaries,
realization math including partial billing and void exclusion).
344/344 backend tests passing (313 pre-existing + 31 new), full
regression run clean.

Not in this commit: frontend UI for invoices/WIP/realization;
independence & conflict-of-interest checks and workpaper review
chains (Q1's other two items).
